From 8cf49c699ce39ae5c7867f5134c89dc14c9e7229 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gourob Saha <gourobsaha2319@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 08:35:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Restructure files to match their content and harden
 DownloadEngine

Structure (no behaviour change, members moved as they were):
- Split the 5,264-line MainForm.cs into MainForm.cs (fields, constructor,
  state) plus Layout / List / Downloads / Add / Settings / Shell / Bridge
  partial files.
- Rename static class Engine to DownloadEngine (like StreamEngine and
  YtDlpEngine); its remote/FTP helpers now live in DownloadEngine.Remote.cs
  and the SharedClient property moved into DownloadEngine.cs.
- Move credential code into Network/CredentialStore.cs, the folder scanner
  into Network/RemoteLister.cs, SSH host keys next to RemoteTransfer.
- Split MediaStreams.cs into MediaModels.cs, MediaParsers.cs (HLS/DASH)
  and MediaDetector.cs.
- Move ScheduleForm and CountdownForm out of Core into UI/ScheduleForms.cs.
- Rename UI/YtDlpPickerForm.cs to YtPickerForm.cs (it holds YtPickerForm).

DownloadEngine fixes:
- Sanitize: reject "." / "..", trailing dots/spaces and Windows device
  names (CON, NUL.txt ...); fall back to the URL name when a server name
  sanitizes to empty (SavePath used to become the folder itself).
- Segment download: 60 s stall timeout, no retry for permanent 4xx errors,
  retry counter restarts after real progress.
- Finish the file with one File.Move(overwrite) instead of delete + move.
